hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-14 = unlines (cons "In cubical mathematics, a square is not a tool for forcing things into line. It is a change: two paths and the witness that they compose. The cube is where the squares live, and *cubus* is the Greek *kubos*, a die, the thing that is thrown. In cubical type theory, the square holds the history of a turning. In the clinic, the square, the norm turned on minds, cuts off whatever doesn't fit it. The same shape is used to remember and to erase." nil)
